Not that I really expect it to result in anything, I just
enjoyed thinking how it might work and how it would be to
play.

The general idea is peace loving, talks to animals (those
monsters that respect Elbereth), a poor fighter, a poor
offensive spell caster, good at escape and use of pets to
assist.

Lawful or neutral, human, dwarf or gnome.

Weapons where skills could be advanced would be those that
might be fashioned in the wild like club, sling, bow, spear,
knife, staff, axe, unicorn horn, bullwhip or boomerang.

Other skills that could be gained would be riding and bare
handed combat.

Spell classes would be enchantment, healing, escape and
divination, with a special ability at charm monster.

No iron armor and no gold. Gold entering inventory or
wearing (putting on, not continuing to wear) iron armor
would anger your god and break the conduct.

The really special talent the Beastmaster would have would
be chatting with monsters. Chatting with a monster (who
respects Elbereth) might tame a peaceful monster or frighten
a hostile monster. The chance would depend on XL and wisdom.
Success with monsters at 1/2 your XL or less would be
excellent and success with monsters higher than your XL
would be pitiful. Iron armor worn or gold in inventory would
reduce the chances. If polymorphed into a monster form,
chatting would automatically tame other monsters of that
type.

Intrinsics would be XL1 stealth, XL 7 searching, XL12
warning and XL17 polymorph control.

The quest artifact would be a magic harp, subject to normal
charging rules. It would grant magic resistance, telepathy
and 1/2 physical damage when carried and act like a scroll
of remove curse when invoked.

The starting inventory would be:
club, staff or bullwhip randomly selected and with some
enchantment.
sling and flintstones or boomerang, randomly, with some
enchantment.
leather armor
fruits
tripe
either a blessed eucalyptus leaf or a magic whistle, not
sure
level one spellbook
stethoscope
leash
saddle

Sound different enough to be interesting?
